  "caseId": "case16",
  "description": "A ticked row carrying neither U nor D: the WHEN OTHER arm at :210-214. 'Invalid selection. Valid values are U and D' is painted and the cursor is placed, but - and this is the whole point of the case - NO error flag is raised, so PROCESS-ENTER-KEY does not return: it falls through to :218 and pages forward anyway, and the complaint arrives together with a freshly listed page. The twenty-five-record file is used deliberately: over ten records the look-ahead READNEXT at :311 would reach the end of the file and overwrite WS-MESSAGE with 'You have reached the bottom of the page...', hiding the very message this case exists to pin. Because the tick is not acted on, CDEMO-CU00-USR-SEL-FLG and CDEMO-CU00-USR-SELECTED are carried forward holding the rejected values rather than being cleared.",
